.TH SCAN_PB_TAG 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
scan_pb_tag \- Scan a Protocol Buffers tag from a string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>

.IB size_t
.IB scan_pb_tag(const char* in, size_t len, size_t* fieldno, unsigned char* type);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBscan_pb_tag\fR function scans a Protocol Buffers tag from a given string and extracts the field number and type.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB in
The input string containing the Protocol Buffers tag.
.TP
.IB len
The length of the input string.
.TP
.IB fieldno
The destination where the field number will be stored.
.TP
.IB type
The destination where the type will be stored.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters processed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBscan_pb_tag\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>

int main() {
    const char* tag = "\x1a";
    size_t fieldno, length;
    unsigned char type;
    length = scan_pb_tag(tag, 1, &fieldno, &type);
    printf("Field number: %zu\n", fieldno);
    printf("Type: %d\n", type);
    printf("Length processed: %zu\n", length);
    return 0;
}
.nef